1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:05,255
[OLIVER]<i> How did you know</i>
<i>that I wanted this game?</i>

2
00:00:05,338 --> 00:00:10,093
[BEA] <i>Papa told me,</i>
<i>so since I got my first paycheck today,</i>

3
00:00:10,176 --> 00:00:12,220
<i>I thought of gifting it to you.</i>

4
00:00:12,303 --> 00:00:15,932
[OLIVER] <i>Thank you, Bea.</i>
<i>I love you so, so, so much!</i>

5
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:17,892
[BEA]<i> Wow! You love me</i>
<i>just because of that?</i>

6
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:19,352
[OLIVER] <i>Thank you.</i>

7
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:21,438
- [BEA] <i>Welcome.</i>
- [OLIVER] <i>I love you.</i>

8
00:00:23,022 --> 00:00:24,274
<i>Seriously?</i>

9
00:00:24,357 --> 00:00:25,608
<i>- You're unbelievable!</i>
<i>- Billy.</i>

10
00:00:25,692 --> 00:00:27,861
- <i>You've got some nerve!</i>
<i>- Billy! Billy!</i>

11
00:00:27,944 --> 00:00:30,196
<i>- Leave my brother alone!</i>
<i>- Stay there, Oliver.</i>

12
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,906
<i>- How dare you come here?!</i>
<i>- Billy, stop!</i>

13
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:33,825
<i>- What else do you want, huh?!</i>
<i>- Billy. Billy!</i>

14
00:00:33,908 --> 00:00:35,827
<i>- Get out! Leave!</i>
- <i>Billy!</i>

15
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,996
<i>Don't ever come back here! Get out!</i>

16
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:39,998
<i>- I have no bad intentions.</i>
<i>- Billy!</i>

17
00:00:40,081 --> 00:00:41,374
[BILLY] <i>Oliver, stay away from her.</i>

18
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:42,959
<i>I said stay away from her!</i>

19
00:00:43,042 --> 00:00:45,462
<i>She's not doing anything wrong to you.</i>

20
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:46,921
<i>I'm just protecting you.</i>

21
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:48,381
<i>Listen to me. I'm your sister, aren't I?</i>

22
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:49,758
<i>Come here now.</i>

23
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:50,842
<i>- She's a bad person!</i>
<i>- Billy!</i>

24
00:00:50,925 --> 00:00:52,218
<i>- Stay away from her!</i>
<i>- Billy!</i>

25
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:53,720
<i>- Come here!</i>
<i>- I don't want to!</i>

26
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:55,138
<i>Stop! You're hurting Oliver!</i>

27
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:57,057
<i>Come here.</i>

28
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:59,601
<i>You're the one turning into</i>
<i>a bad person, Billy.</i>

29
00:00:59,684 --> 00:01:02,312
<i>After everything I did for you?!</i>

30
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:03,521
<i>Fine!</i>

31
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:04,898
<i>Okay, go. Go with her!</i>

32
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,066
<i>- Go with her!</i>
<i>- Billy. Billy!</i>

33
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:07,609
<i>You want to be with her? Then go!</i>

34
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:10,028
<i>One less problem for me to worry about!</i>

35
00:01:10,111 --> 00:01:12,363
- [PRECIOUS] <i>You've gone too far!</i>
- [BILLY]<i> No, Auntie!</i>

36
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:13,615
<i>Go on, take her side!</i>

37
00:01:13,698 --> 00:01:15,283
<i>Leave me!</i>

38
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:18,119
<i>You deserve each other!</i>

39
00:01:18,203 --> 00:01:21,039
[WAILS]

40
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:25,960
[WAILING]

41
00:01:26,586 --> 00:01:27,962
[GLASS SHATTERING]

42
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:29,214
[KEEPS WAILING]

43
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:32,926
[CRIES]

44
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:39,724
<i>Why did you let Bea inside our house?</i>

45
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:42,894
<i>I didn't want to, Billy.</i>

46
00:01:42,977 --> 00:01:45,063
<i>Everything she did to us…</i>

47
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:48,566
<i>You're just going to forget it</i>
<i>like nothing happened?</i>

48
00:01:52,403 --> 00:01:55,740
<i>Am I really the one</i>
<i>in the wrong here, Auntie?</i>

49
00:01:55,824 --> 00:01:58,326
<i>I remember where I saw Billy as a kid.</i>

50
00:01:58,409 --> 00:02:00,203
<i>On the night of Jade's accident.</i>

51
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:03,748
<i>Billy was the one who hit Jade with a car!</i>

52
00:02:03,832 --> 00:02:05,250
<i>Dino.</i>

53
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:09,879
<i>Billy was the one</i>
<i>driving the car that hit Jade.</i>

54
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:12,173
<i>Billy, can you slow down?</i>

55
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:15,135
<i>The company is in trouble.</i>

56
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:17,637
- <i>But you're not alone.</i>
- [BILLY] <i>You sure about that?</i>

57
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:21,099
<i>Where are the people</i>
<i>I expect to help me now?</i>

58
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:23,476
<i>Where are they now when I need them most?</i>

59
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,061
<i>Where are you?</i>

60
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:27,522
<i>You think you can just come back</i>
<i>whenever you want?</i>

61
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:37,699
[CAR BEEPS]

62
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:45,540
[PHONE RINGS]

63
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:47,417
[GRUNTS]

64
00:02:49,586 --> 00:02:50,753
Damn it.

65
00:02:51,796 --> 00:02:53,047
[INHALES SHARPLY]

66
00:02:54,382 --> 00:02:56,009
- [SEAT BELT THUDS]
- [EXHALES DEEPLY]

67
00:02:56,092 --> 00:02:59,262
[RINGING CONTINUES]

68
00:03:00,597 --> 00:03:03,266
Hello? Who is this?

69
00:03:03,349 --> 00:03:06,060
[MODULATED VOICE]
<i>You don't know me, but I know who you are.</i>

70
00:03:07,562 --> 00:03:09,063
<i>I know what you've done in the past.</i>

71
00:03:09,147 --> 00:03:10,231
What?!

72
00:03:10,315 --> 00:03:11,566
<i>You killed someone.</i>

73
00:03:12,066 --> 00:03:15,737
<i>June 18, 2013, at around 8:00 p.m.</i>

74
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:19,657
<i>It was raining heavily</i>
<i>and the road was dark.</i>

75
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:21,993
<i>You ran over a woman,</i>

76
00:03:22,076 --> 00:03:23,870
<i>and you didn't help her.</i>

77
00:03:24,704 --> 00:03:26,831
<i>You killed Jade Valentin.</i>

78
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:30,919
<i>You're a murderer, Benilda Cariño.</i>

79
00:03:31,711 --> 00:03:34,005
<i>If you don't want me</i>
<i>to expose your secret,</i>

80
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:35,506
<i>call me.</i>

81
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:36,966
<i>Let's talk.</i>

82
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:38,259
Is this a scam?

83
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:39,594
A prank?

84
00:03:40,678 --> 00:03:43,598
Leave me alone,
or I'll report you to the police.

85
00:03:43,681 --> 00:03:45,558
<i>I know that your business</i>
<i>is struggling right now.</i>

86
00:03:46,684 --> 00:03:48,728
But you'll get yourself in deeper trouble

87
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:51,439
when I spread what I know about you.

88
00:03:51,522 --> 00:03:53,149
Who are you?

89
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:54,984
What the hell are you talking about?!

90
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:57,820
Are you denying it?
That you ran over someone in the past?

91
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:01,574
<i>If you don't want the whole world</i>

92
00:04:01,658 --> 00:04:02,867
and your best friend to know

93
00:04:02,951 --> 00:04:05,954
that you're the one who killed his mom,

94
00:04:06,037 --> 00:04:08,289
you're going to give me
three million pesos.

95
00:04:08,373 --> 00:04:11,626
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:04:11,709 --> 00:04:12,794
Bea?

97
00:04:14,712 --> 00:04:15,964
Bea, it's you, isn't it?

98
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:18,466
Call me again

99
00:04:18,549 --> 00:04:20,802
and make sure you have my 3 million.

100
00:04:21,344 --> 00:04:22,679
- Hello? Who's--
- [LINE DISCONNECTS]

101
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:24,764
Who are you?! Hello?!

102
00:04:24,847 --> 00:04:25,807
Hello?!

103
00:04:25,890 --> 00:04:28,393
[LINE DISCONNECTING]

104
00:04:31,062 --> 00:04:31,980
[PHONE THUDS]

105
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:36,776
[TENSE MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

106
00:04:38,569 --> 00:04:44,909
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

107
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:45,470
[SIGHS] So? Do you think
she's going to do it?

108
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:47,430
Well, if she doesn't,

109
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:50,475
I'll tell everyone that she's a murderer.

110
00:05:50,558 --> 00:05:54,729
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

111
00:05:54,812 --> 00:05:56,064
Are you okay?

112
00:05:57,523 --> 00:05:59,025
That probably hurts.

113
00:05:59,650 --> 00:06:00,985
Many years have passed,

114
00:06:01,069 --> 00:06:04,072
but you only found out now
who killed Jade.

115
00:06:05,114 --> 00:06:07,408
It won't bring back Jade.

116
00:06:08,076 --> 00:06:10,369
So let's just make money off of it.

117
00:06:12,330 --> 00:06:16,959
Uh… Don't worry. We will
get justice for Jade's death.

118
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:21,464
Don't you want to hold
Benilda Cariño accountable?

119
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:22,715
Of course I want to.

120
00:06:23,299 --> 00:06:25,676
But given our current situation,

121
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:27,720
getting money is my priority.

122
00:06:27,804 --> 00:06:32,767
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

123
00:06:35,686 --> 00:06:39,774
Marj was having an anxiety attack,
so I told her to go home.

124
00:06:40,358 --> 00:06:41,859
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

125
00:06:43,027 --> 00:06:45,947
I want to apologize on Billy's behalf.

126
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:48,574
Try to understand her, guys.

127
00:06:49,408 --> 00:06:51,744
You know that she has a lot on her plate.

128
00:06:52,578 --> 00:06:54,997
But, Jordan, this is too much.

129
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:57,834
It's not like we're just slacking off.

130
00:06:57,917 --> 00:07:00,044
We're also trying to do something.

131
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,505
And outside working hours,

132
00:07:02,588 --> 00:07:04,590
we can't talk to her
without her getting angry.

133
00:07:04,674 --> 00:07:07,426
We're just trying to sympathize.

134
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:08,678
Also…

135
00:07:09,679 --> 00:07:11,597
we're worried about her.

136
00:07:11,681 --> 00:07:13,266
I understand you, guys.

137
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:15,476
But right now,

138
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:18,563
Billy needs us the most.

139
00:07:20,606 --> 00:07:22,942
We've all enjoyed being by her side

140
00:07:23,025 --> 00:07:24,402
when she's at her highest.

141
00:07:25,236 --> 00:07:27,488
Let's not abandon her
when she's at her lowest.

142
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:31,033
- Okay?
- Sounds good.

143
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:40,042
[DISTORTED VOICE] <i>If you don't want</i>
<i>the whole world and your best friend</i>

144
00:07:40,126 --> 00:07:43,171
<i>to know that you're the one</i>
<i>who killed his mom,</i>

145
00:07:43,254 --> 00:07:45,506
<i>you're going to give me</i>
<i>three million pesos.</i>

146
00:07:45,590 --> 00:07:52,430
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

147
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:58,144
[CAR DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

148
00:07:58,853 --> 00:07:59,812
Bea!

149
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:02,773
What's so funny?!

150
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:03,983
Are you happy now?!

151
00:08:04,775 --> 00:08:05,943
You're happy?

152
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:08,362
God, you're really making sure
I lose everything, aren't you?!

153
00:08:09,363 --> 00:08:11,574
Huh? W-What are you saying?

154
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,784
First, Dad.

155
00:08:13,868 --> 00:08:16,370
Then Auntie Pres. Then Oliver.

156
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:18,164
Now Jordan?

157
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:20,166
You want to ruin our friendship?

158
00:08:20,249 --> 00:08:22,376
Is that why you've resorted to blackmail?!

159
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:24,295
Billy, I don't know
what you're talking about.

160
00:08:24,378 --> 00:08:26,506
I have no idea.

161
00:08:28,257 --> 00:08:29,342
Are you okay?

162
00:08:29,425 --> 00:08:30,718
What's going on?

163
00:08:30,801 --> 00:08:32,261
What's going on?!

164
00:08:34,138 --> 00:08:35,431
[BREATHES SHARPLY]

165
00:08:37,683 --> 00:08:38,809
Look at me.

166
00:08:40,353 --> 00:08:41,938
Look at me!

167
00:08:42,021 --> 00:08:43,064
Look!

168
00:08:43,147 --> 00:08:48,486
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

169
00:08:48,569 --> 00:08:51,572
You did this to me!

170
00:08:52,114 --> 00:08:54,116
[INHALES SHARPLY] You happened!

171
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,535
[SOBS]

172
00:08:56,244 --> 00:08:59,664
[SOBBING]

173
00:09:14,595 --> 00:09:16,389
[LINE RINGING]

174
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:19,850
Send the money tomorrow morning.

175
00:09:19,934 --> 00:09:23,062
I'll send you the time
and the exact location.

176
00:09:23,145 --> 00:09:24,730
Oh, really?

177
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:27,191
Really? You really won't stop?

178
00:09:28,109 --> 00:09:31,070
Whatever you do,
you won't get a cent from me!

179
00:09:31,153 --> 00:09:33,739
You have to pay for what you did.

180
00:09:34,323 --> 00:09:36,909
You're lucky all you have to do is pay up.

181
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:38,286
Make your choice.

182
00:09:38,369 --> 00:09:40,246
Pay up or jail time?

183
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:42,039
I never committed a crime.

184
00:09:42,123 --> 00:09:43,624
I didn't kill anyone, Bea.

185
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:46,502
So can you just leave me alone?!

186
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:47,962
[CALL DROPS]

187
00:09:49,672 --> 00:09:51,757
- Who is Bea?
- How would I know?

188
00:09:52,341 --> 00:09:53,676
Oliver.

189
00:09:55,303 --> 00:09:56,470
B-Billy?

190
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:57,555
Hey.

191
00:09:58,598 --> 00:10:00,641
- Why are you acting that way?
- [CHAIR SCRAPES]

192
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:02,560
- Huh? Why?
- [PRECIOUS] Billy, Billy.

193
00:10:02,643 --> 00:10:04,645
Oliver, are you okay? Are you both okay?

194
00:10:04,729 --> 00:10:07,148
Billy. Do you need anything?

195
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:08,608
What's this?

196
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:10,651
I--

197
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:12,194
Billy.

198
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:14,196
Billy! Billy!

199
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:15,281
Billy.

200
00:10:15,364 --> 00:10:18,492
Billy… Billy, I know you're tired.

201
00:10:18,576 --> 00:10:19,702
Take a break for a while.

202
00:10:19,785 --> 00:10:21,621
What's all this, Auntie?

203
00:10:21,704 --> 00:10:23,789
Why do you seem so worried about Oliver?

204
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:26,667
It's not that. I'm sorry.

205
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:28,419
But he's getting scared of you.

206
00:10:28,502 --> 00:10:31,297
Scared? Of me?

207
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:34,425
Because I want to protect him from Bea?

208
00:10:34,508 --> 00:10:35,509
But why--

209
00:10:35,593 --> 00:10:37,595
What are you protecting him from?

210
00:10:37,678 --> 00:10:40,806
Billy, Bea is keeping her distance.

211
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:42,475
Someone called me, Auntie Pres!

212
00:10:42,558 --> 00:10:44,852
They were asking for money and claiming

213
00:10:44,935 --> 00:10:47,897
that I was the one
who killed Jordan's mom!

214
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:51,359
They said they'd expose me
if I didn't pay up.

215
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:53,569
Who else would do that?

216
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:57,531
Who else would go out of their way
to ruin our lives?

217
00:10:58,449 --> 00:11:00,117
It has to be Bea, right?

218
00:11:00,201 --> 00:11:05,998
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

219
00:11:08,084 --> 00:11:12,254
[PRECIOUS] Billy, are you sure
it was really Bea?

220
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:13,339
I mean,

221
00:11:13,422 --> 00:11:16,384
how would Bea even come up
with a story like that?

222
00:11:16,467 --> 00:11:17,802
Think about it.

223
00:11:17,885 --> 00:11:24,725
She even knows about the night
you rushed your mom to the hospital.

224
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:26,977
She even knows which street you took.

225
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:31,982
And she connected all that
to Jordan's mom's death?

226
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,484
Come on, Auntie.

227
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:37,530
It's like you don't know
what that woman is capable of.

228
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:40,699
Didn't she already try
to bleed me dry once already?

229
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:43,577
She even used Peter,
who was supposed to be our investor.

230
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:47,498
So she's definitely capable
of pulling this again.

231
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:52,628
But Billy, are you sure
you remember that night right?

232
00:11:52,711 --> 00:11:55,756
You didn't hit anyone that night, did you?

233
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,174
[SLAMS HANDS ON TABLE]

234
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:59,218
What kind of question is that, Auntie?

235
00:12:00,469 --> 00:12:02,638
What? Is that what you think of me now?

236
00:12:02,721 --> 00:12:04,723
That I'm a murderer?

237
00:12:06,892 --> 00:12:13,399
Billy, I'm just wondering
how Bea came up with all this.

238
00:12:13,482 --> 00:12:15,943
- If it really is Bea--
- It is Bea, Auntie!

239
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:18,237
It's Bea! I know it's her!

240
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:23,576
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

241
00:12:23,659 --> 00:12:28,497
Billy, if Jordan doesn't know yet,
you should tell him.

242
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:31,667
It concerns his mother.

243
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:34,170
What for?

244
00:12:35,087 --> 00:12:37,590
So she can ruin
my friendship with him too?

245
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:44,221
We know what my friend has been through
ever since he lost his mom, Auntie.

246
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:46,640
He carries that pain every day.

247
00:12:48,434 --> 00:12:51,854
He doesn't need to hear about
that woman's latest stunt.

248
00:12:56,817 --> 00:13:02,615
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

249
00:13:05,159 --> 00:13:06,952
[SEATBELT CLICKS]

250
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:09,538
[ENGINE STARTS]

251
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:11,415
[GEAR CRANKS]

252
00:13:12,416 --> 00:13:17,713
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

253
00:13:22,009 --> 00:13:23,886
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [THUD]

254
00:13:23,969 --> 00:13:29,058
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

255
00:13:42,696 --> 00:13:44,156
[PHONE CHIMES]

256
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:49,870
3 MILLION PESOS IN CASH.
TOMORROW, 10 AM.

257
00:13:49,954 --> 00:13:52,081
46 MABINI STREET,
AT THE ABANDONED AUTO SHOP.

258
00:13:52,164 --> 00:13:54,333
DON'T EVEN THINK ABOUT
BRINGING THE COPS.

259
00:13:54,416 --> 00:14:01,423
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

260
00:14:15,688 --> 00:14:17,189
What?

261
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:19,567
Me? But, Pa…

262
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:21,318
Where was I back then?

263
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:23,696
And besides…

264
00:14:24,488 --> 00:14:29,577
Did I know any of those details
about that night? No.

265
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:32,037
Pa, please believe me.

266
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:34,707
I'm really telling the truth this time.

267
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:36,709
I had nothing to do with it.

268
00:14:36,792 --> 00:14:38,878
I know you're telling the truth.

269
00:14:38,961 --> 00:14:43,132
But I hope you can understand
why Billy is suspicious of you.

270
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:46,010
Of course.

271
00:14:46,093 --> 00:14:48,804
I know where Billy's coming from.

272
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:52,224
[SIGHS HEAVILY]
I'll try talking to her.

273
00:14:53,434 --> 00:14:54,518
You know what?

274
00:14:55,477 --> 00:14:58,689
Whoever's extorting her, I'm sure…

275
00:15:00,357 --> 00:15:02,651
that they intend to put her in danger.

276
00:15:13,287 --> 00:15:15,205
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

277
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:18,125
[GATE CREAKS OPEN, CLOSES]

278
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:25,007
[TRICYCLE ENGINE HUMMING]

279
00:15:25,090 --> 00:15:26,467
[MAN] Need a tricycle, ma'am?

280
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:31,430
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

281
00:15:31,513 --> 00:15:32,765
[MAN] Where are you headed?

282
00:15:38,729 --> 00:15:43,901
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

283
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:02,628
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

284
00:16:18,143 --> 00:16:23,440
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

285
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:42,376
[KNOCKS ON CAR DOOR]

286
00:16:45,212 --> 00:16:46,380
Billy.

287
00:16:47,965 --> 00:16:49,341
What are you doing here?

288
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:54,138
Tell your accomplice that
I will never give you any money.

289
00:16:56,265 --> 00:16:57,683
Accomplice?

290
00:16:58,934 --> 00:17:01,687
What do I have to do to prove that
I'm not the one doing it?

291
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:03,188
Just admit it!

292
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:07,026
Billy, I'm trying to change!

293
00:17:07,109 --> 00:17:11,196
I want to make up for all the things
my mother and I did to you.

294
00:17:11,989 --> 00:17:13,782
I really don't know
what you're talking about.

295
00:17:13,866 --> 00:17:17,077
I know it's hard to believe me, but

296
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:19,997
please believe me, I don't know anything!

297
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:26,670
It's hard to trust someone
who's lied to you over and over.

298
00:17:30,924 --> 00:17:33,010
The truth will come out eventually.

299
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:41,351
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

300
00:17:44,605 --> 00:17:47,274
Have you traced the number I gave you?

301
00:17:47,357 --> 00:17:49,318
[OFFICER] <i>Ma'am, it's not that easy.</i>

302
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:51,612
So what? There's nothing
you can do about it again?

303
00:17:51,695 --> 00:17:54,656
[OFFICER] <i>We're doing</i>
<i>everything we can, ma'am.</i>

304
00:17:57,159 --> 00:18:03,207
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

305
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:06,543
[CHARM] Oh… Chief!

306
00:18:06,627 --> 00:18:08,170
I sent you an email

307
00:18:08,253 --> 00:18:12,299
with the revised proposal
for our potential advertisers.

308
00:18:12,382 --> 00:18:14,218
It's still waiting for your approval.

309
00:18:14,301 --> 00:18:15,761
Have you had a chance to look at it?

310
00:18:15,844 --> 00:18:18,097
Can it wait, Charm?!

311
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:21,934
Oh. Okay.

312
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:32,194
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

313
00:18:32,277 --> 00:18:33,821
[PHONE CHIMES]

314
00:18:38,408 --> 00:18:40,244
<i>It's time for the whole world to know</i>

315
00:18:40,327 --> 00:18:43,872
<i>that LoveList CEO</i>
<i>Billy Cariño is a criminal.</i>

316
00:18:43,956 --> 00:18:47,876
<i>June 18, 2013, at 8:30 p.m.,</i>

317
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:50,879
<i>on Feliciano Street, Barangay Del Mundo.</i>

318
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:54,550
<i>She killed Jade Valentin in a hit-and-run.</i>

319
00:18:54,633 --> 00:18:57,803
<i>She was the mother</i>
<i>of Billy's friend, Jordan Valentin.</i>

320
00:18:57,886 --> 00:18:59,263
<i>I saw it with my own eyes.</i>

321
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:01,140
<i>You were the one</i>
<i>who killed her, Billy Cariño!</i>

322
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:03,433
<i>You're a murderer! You're a criminal!</i>

323
00:19:03,517 --> 00:19:04,977
<i>You have to face justice!</i>

324
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:07,896
<i>You have to pay for what you've done!</i>

325
00:19:07,980 --> 00:19:13,485
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

326
00:19:26,498 --> 00:19:27,791
<i>Jordan.</i>

327
00:19:28,917 --> 00:19:31,253
<i>Are you really going to</i>
<i>throw everything away?</i>

328
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:33,797
<i>Yes, I would.</i>

329
00:19:34,548 --> 00:19:36,800
<i>Okay? Billy needs me.</i>

330
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:37,801
<i>Okay?</i>

331
00:19:40,345 --> 00:19:41,763
<i>Someone's blackmailing me.</i>

332
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:43,223
<i>Since when?</i>

333
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:46,602
<i>And why didn't you tell me right away?</i>

334
00:19:47,519 --> 00:19:48,812
<i>Because…</i>

335
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:51,023
<i>Because I didn't want</i>
<i>you getting dragged into this.</i>

336
00:19:51,106 --> 00:19:54,568
<i>- I didn't want you to get hurt.</i>
<i>- Okay. Billy, relax, relax.</i>

337
00:19:54,651 --> 00:19:56,570
<i>I don't understand.</i>

338
00:19:56,653 --> 00:19:58,197
<i>Why would I get hurt?</i>

339
00:20:01,366 --> 00:20:06,622
<i>The street where your mom was found…</i>

340
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:09,374
<i>I drove down that same street.</i>

341
00:20:10,542 --> 00:20:12,586
[BILLY SOBBING, BREATHES SHAKILY]

342
00:20:12,669 --> 00:20:14,379
<i>Are you sure it's the same street?</i>

343
00:20:16,298 --> 00:20:20,260
<i>Dude, you were too young</i>
<i>to remember back then, okay?</i>

344
00:20:21,762 --> 00:20:24,473
<i>You might be remembering it wrong.</i>

345
00:20:24,556 --> 00:20:27,226
- [RAIN POURING]
- [BREATH QUIVERING]

346
00:20:28,352 --> 00:20:35,317
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [BREATHING HEAVILY]

347
00:20:46,119 --> 00:20:49,289
[SOBBING]

348
00:20:54,711 --> 00:20:57,172
- [SOBS, MUMBLING INCOHERENTLY]
- [LIGHTNING CRACKS]

349
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:01,927
[BREATHING SHAKILY]

350
00:21:03,512 --> 00:21:05,639
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

351
00:21:05,722 --> 00:21:11,645
[PANICKED BREATHING]
